ROLE: You make literal edits to one TypeScript file.

CONTEXT: In `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src/runtime/client.ts`, `RuntimeClient.close()` returns at once when no child process exists yet. If it runs while `spawn()` is still awaiting `ensurePython()`, that startup carries on afterwards and spawns a Python runtime nobody will close.

ACTION: Re-read the file. Make exactly these edits and nothing else.

1. Replace the line `  private broken = false;` with these lines:

  private broken = false;
  // Set by close(); a startup still provisioning when it is set must not spawn.
  private closed = false;

2. In `private async spawn()`, directly after the closing `}` of the `try { pythonPath = await this.ensurePython(); } catch (err) { ... return; }` block, and before the line that starts `    const runtimeScript = resolvePath(`, insert:

    if (this.closed) {
      log("closed before the runtime started; not spawning");
      return;
    }

3. In `async close()`, replace these lines:

  async close(): Promise<void> {
    const child = this.child;

with:

  async close(): Promise<void> {
    this.closed = true;
    const child = this.child;

FORMAT: Then run `cd .skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime && bunx tsc --noEmit; echo typecheck-exit=$?` and print the output verbatim, nothing else.
